      <description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/d93546fa061fd0241e22f9417e2ae0f221286408.png?auto=compress,format&amp;h=340&amp;w=1200&amp;s=6d60dbf51d1162e933a168f919d46318"&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/2749cb39feab1d86fe3f5eba9a22f2cd009348ac.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=crop&amp;h=600&amp;w=1200&amp;s=eadd4810a8371ebcee50a298486f2dce"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Become the world’s greatest football star&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When Japan’s national football team ranked low at the 2018 World Cup, they knew something needed to be done. Enter Yoichi Isagi, the hero of &lt;em&gt;Blue Lock&lt;/em&gt;, Muneyuki Kaneshiro and Yusuke Nomura’s shonen manga series about a cutthroat football training program designed to create the best striker in the world! Now, you can get all currently published digital volumes of &lt;em&gt;Blue Lock&lt;/em&gt; in one bundle, including volumes of the main series up to #38, redemption code for #39 on kodansha.us, and seven volumes of prequel miniseries &lt;em&gt;Episode Nagi&lt;/em&gt; by Kota Sannomiya, Muneyuki Kaneshiro and Yusuke Nomura! Dive into a manga series perfect for football fans and shonen readers alike! Get these manga ebooks now at the price of your choosing, and support BINC with your purchase!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#0"&gt;Pay $5 to unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol2"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol3"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol2"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol1"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol1"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bt10"&gt;Pay $10 or more to also unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol4"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol3"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol7"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol6"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol5"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol4"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bt20"&gt;Pay $20 or more to also unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol5"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol16"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol15"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol14"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol13"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol12"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol11"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol10"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol9"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol8"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bt30"&gt;Pay $30 or more to also unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol7"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_episodenagi_vol6"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol38"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 38&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol37"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol36"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol35"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 35&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol34"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 34&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol33"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 33&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol32"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 32&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol31"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 31&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol30"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol29"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol28"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol27"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol26"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol25"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol24"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol23"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 23&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol22"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 22&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol21"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol20"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol19"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol18"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bluelock_vol17"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 id="0"&gt;Pay $5 to unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol2"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol2" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol2_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=4fd46e634af5fb2ce54a5075d4aab039a861a63ebd8d10004045ea2fa9f3ba1b"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/27322c3765b55f8bc13b4d86b18a9bfb6dbad7f8.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=c087ef2a01de6ee4ef8de038a3ed0a3d"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roused by Ego's speech at orientation, Reo jumped head-first into the Blue Lock program…and dragged Nagi in kicking and screaming. Now the real work begins as Ego announces their next test, the “first selection.” In this round-robin battle between the members of wing five, it's not just about being on the winning team; the top scorers also get a goal bonus. Let the clash of massive egos begin!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol3"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol3" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol3_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=746a52b3e109a883895d4a721c828cad42a1574f194d9af0b1ab792caea9c4a0"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/d7ace7fd5068d860513a1ada33bba04d013b3e2f.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=44d78b4944ddc52baf10d8eb57c8190d"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Savoring the sweet taste of victory against Team Y, Team Z is pumped to face their next opponent in the first selection round-robin tournament-Team W! But cracks begin to show within the shaky bonds of Team Z, and internal fears freeze players in their tracks on the field. In the face of Team W's powerful aces, the Wanima twins, will Team Z be able to come together in time to escape defeat?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol2"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol2" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol2_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=835f66c93cdd9d15adea94688da4b37f466aab6c6f589be25ae747dd9b14fdad"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/3f2251972538fe912dc1727b56c75ba296d51647.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=0c51646c9ac45ba54f82ce9a759cb0c2"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yoichi Isagi, one of three hundred high school soccer players, is in Team Z-the lowest ranked group in the controversial training facility, Blue Lock, where the aim is to create Japan's best striker. To survive their first round-robin tournament, Isagi's Team Z will need to find a way to use their unique “weapons,” while struggling through a clash of egos. But Isagi grapples to understand what his strength is as a striker…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol1"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol1" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol1_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=0b875308795043e9e60a985fbd684565e948292fcaf4a52d4ef208e7477c9cf9"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/93f40c497d312dce2f6a6135038ca11ae5d138c0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5792c1f49e21d87e69bd8550dbc3572b"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Second-year high school student Reo Mikage wants nothing more than to escape his illustrious family's shadow by becoming a soccer star and winning the World Cup. The only thing that's missing is a talented diamond in the rough who can help him achieve his dream. That's when he sets his sights on Seishiro Nagi, a notorious slacker whose quick reflexes are the only hint of athletic ability. Can Reo find the switch to awaken the beast inside Nagi?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol1"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol1" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol1_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=240d989efeb5c31975ac9b1b746a601949245ce03d59539ad9d2cfb887a8442c"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/9247625df4e4f7b4a727f823dcc07831dabb46ec.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=cd9b847c7d4fae75eadb706194ef2ae2"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;After a disastrous defeat at the 2018 World Cup, Japan's team struggles to regroup. But what's missing? An absolute Ace Striker, who can guide them to the win. The Japan Football Union is hell-bent on creating a striker who hungers for goals and thirsts for victory, and who can be the decisive instrument in turning around a losing match...and to do so, they've gathered 300 of Japan's best and brightest youth players. Who will emerge to lead the team...and will they be able to out-muscle and out-ego everyone who stands in their way?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt10"&gt;Pay $10 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol4"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol4" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol4_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=44fdce1d650272556d917c55b0bffc9c151cd524f546bf9033d450c64d657fec"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ba600c61938c042aaf8bb3a7ddbddd464b1bb965.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=9e40927819dafb22f27dc21f7f5d225e"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;After getting “stolen” by Isagi's team, Nagi finds himself torn between his newly awakened ego and his friendship with Reo. Can the two friends ever repair their relationship after Nagi's apparent betrayal? That question gets put to the test as Nagi, Isagi, and Barou face off against Reo, Kunigami, and Chigiri for a chance to clear the Second Selection. Reo will do whatever it takes to steal Nagi back…but will it be enough?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol3"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol3" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol3_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=739b611092bddf187a948110b51202c0275f13b0c864395c8353e1934cd3e17d"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/691ef294355677a3cf828598f3dbc41bc18a4284.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=8552b9a82465a75ed75b0dd2c47df6ac"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to the triple threat of Nagi, Reo, and Zantetsu, Team V has breezed through each round of the First Selection. That is, until they come up against Team Z and Yoichi Isagi. Isagi's passion for the game suddenly has Nagi questioning everything: What makes him push himself so hard? What does soccer mean to him? Why not just give up? Farewell ennui, hello ego... It's time for the slacker to finally awaken!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol7"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol7" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol7_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=586217549b250e6dbb38a573d2bc9e16168c0118d789cf944ef04bdddb66ebb3"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/8811f70692640c6f28be1bbfd37e2b445c733592.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=53aa2cc02327d7ce3e755eb821c3700c"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the second selection's rival battles-where the winners can choose one player from the losing team-Isagi and Nagi have just lost Bachira to Rin Itoshi and the other top strikers. Now they must prove the strength of their individual abilities in a fight against Shouei Barou, the top scoring player in Wing 5. If they lose, they'll be at risk of disqualification… As Isagi takes the fight to King Barou, he's aiming to end up on the side of the prodigies!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol6"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol6" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol6_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=b556884c0bf24d18d92e1a349feb6e34a5e47aef309b4bf1d9c6db9c5b778aa5"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/4a75d37b5d275ca71208130ed3989cd13d0e357c.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=c9ab897e819f4165511b0437fb9a6795"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;After Isagi and the rest of Team Z clear the first selection round, they split up to face the second selection individually. Waiting beyond the first door is Blue Lock Man, a cutting-edge goalkeeping AI system. A new group of incredible strikers and shocking rules await Isagi in the second selection round…!!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol5"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol5" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol5_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=5c07f5a884bc6b5aa90bea34be2804b76b439364b950be57ad26e65c44a69a55"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ac1aa47aa07982c4e599480697552cfa74db61dc.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=31ef1a3b291633478c7ebc68f78ca543"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the face of Team V, Team Z has managed to catch up 3-3 with fifteen minutes remaining. Amid this tense environment, all the players seek their “awakening” that will take their skills to the next level… Will they manage to beat Team V and qualify for the next selection-or will they be stuck on the playing field with nowhere to go?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol4"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol4" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol4_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=b6e60319346eefbd6067885e5eabd36721d318311cdccb0e3f9c40b86cec024a"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/0d48df92b36bc7434e4446d1e3c162e6fa9df428.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=56cc21023ac795196ca939959ac6d596"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's the final round of the first selection and Team Z needs to win against Team V-the undefeated team of Wing 5-to survive! A triple threat awaits Isagi, including prodigy Seishiro Nagi, who only started playing soccer six months ago. Moreover, Team Z is still one man down after Kuon's brutal betrayal in the previous game. The odds are stacked against them as they enter the pitch, and Isagi and his teammates are becoming painfully aware of how weak they really are. In the end, is it all pointless? Or will desperation triumph over talent?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt20"&gt;Pay $20 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol5"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol5" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol5_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=1647a6c828aa335930f2ebc2a45ad2146dbdf4f788d44ad2dc23c2ecf15d5dcb"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6de5f474dbb5ebc7224f9a76e17fee6babb665d0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=c1e3cb6f3b12b43daa5b69a30439d1be"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Things are looking dire for Nagi following a gut-wrenching loss to Rin's team. With Isagi gone after being stolen, Nagi, Barou, and Chigiri must find a way to claw their way back in the next match. Yet that might be easier said than done. As the trio takes the field against Niko, Zantetsu, and Hiiragi, they soon learn that Hiiragi's fortune-telling abilities are more than just a party trick. How do you beat a guy who can predict your every move?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol16"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol16" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol16_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=71937f53e288dcd03758737940adc4cb0be1b2aefc80ea2001e279a0fd28e8a9"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 16&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ee23e5a064831b0069602aaa2125e43b3d41e67b.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=d29458c27fb695332ae38ad1b67a3e44"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Ryusei Shidou's explosive entrance, the U-20 Japan team has seized the initiative in the second half. Just when things are looking dire for the Blue Lock Eleven, Ego produces his trump card, Shouei Barou. “King Barou” proceeds to rampage across the field, consuming friend and foe alike, but Rin and Isagi won't settle for supporting roles. Let the clash of leading actors begin!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol15"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol15" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol15_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=269abaf7c13c30835d8fa650f99e89144d7e5cd50406a6fcfd45b1f5f1885a04"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 15&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/5a619346d751c477f09a32d008997bad6c2d8e83.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=e2d0967ba175d5e02c1a72c28ca44945"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Rin Itoshi's screamer and some solid defending in the dying minutes of the first half, the Blue Lock Eleven are up 2-1 against the U-20 Japan team. Morale is running low in the U-20 locker room, and things only get worse when Sae Itoshi threatens to leave. Just then, an ominous figure emerges from the wings… The demon striker Ryusei Shidou is finally loose and ready to run rampant!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol14"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol14" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol14_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=a178ce4a3102dd08c5ac47f5b28bfccc956810307ae54d3a18a82e78e55d8712"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/f487757ae09393380961447408fb4db74779abf7.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=338d0e710facd404f2d5ac5b3c9b970d"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The curtain finally rises on the Blue Lock Eleven versus U-20 Japan game. Deprived of their wild-card striker, Shidou, the Blue Lock Eleven must find a way to break through the ironclad defense of the so-called “diamond generation.” Individual battles play out across the field as the Itoshi brothers revisit old rivalries and Isagi goes head-to-head with a fellow “reflexive thinker” on the opposing team…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol13"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol13" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol13_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=6579b9230dc658d4d8bfe0902c8a7df4a3af813e5a2ebc1de1968127defc640a"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 13&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/313c49ff0fca3a2ac8a47790f8f8311ed7869a18.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=4a716a30b4cfef78e64eb09c178035ce"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to a last-minute goal, Isagi manages to prove his worth and earn his teammates' respect in the first match of tryouts. But more matches remain, and Isagi will need to master his new “reflexive thinking” ability to earn a place on the Blue Lock Eleven. The board is almost set… Prepare for the ultimate contest between the Blue Lock strikers' “egoism” and the U-20 Japan team's legendary defense!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol12"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol12" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol12_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=3a0c605206ff1d807e4d23338983eb71bb364e2e76f23824b7823366eab73e39"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 12&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/4f2e2f862d5bf350810018585087e32828cf59eb.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=dbf835f573a9d207ac3c4b6ecc39d10f"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;After making it through the grueling Second Selection, Isagi and the remaining thirty-four strikers prepare for their next challenge, a match against the current U-20 Japan team. At stake: a chance to represent Japan on the world stage as part of the U-20 team. However, with only eleven spots available on the Blue Lock team, Isagi must first clear tryouts if he is to keep his dreams alive. Can he assert his place among the best of the best?!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol11"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol11" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol11_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=243ef572fd7a96ccf154054c75fbf3ade49d49bb3b2877b12d71d14a694294aa"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/2e561b04632024af317eab4870da0327d52097a0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=8505e87b4474f59067fb68297ecfef91"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;With seconds left on the clock, Isagi manages to weave a masterful play-until Rin Itoshi and what seems like a stroke of bad luck deal the definitive blow. But what role does luck really play in a soccer match? Ego is eager to impart his wisdom on the advancing players, with the unknowns of the Third Selection looming just ahead…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol10"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol10" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol10_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=03bf1729cfe5c799c2c51c915087873cdaa245708c912abee106515f63996c29"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/3ba4fffef26db40aa54de2d9eb62763be57f206a.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=4bd2d8a03fe524942df2cc6fdd389326"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The rematch against the Top Three requires all the players to use their “weapons” to the fullest. Isagi has made it his goal to defeat Rin Itoshi and steal back Bachira, but he once again finds himself outclassed by Rin in every area. Can Isagi find a way to devour Rin?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol9"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol9" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol9_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=4302231e7c6c61eece58d887628020c5e0d29ac1d013b55792a38561beda0f53"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/cb891783e2a47f1058d90afb1a643dc09574f0d0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=7bb97600ce7afd0e1a98530344ec6e5f"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Barou's awakening, Isagi's team manages to defeat the trio of Kunigami, Chigiri, and Reo. And the one that Isagi chooses to steal is... The new four-man team sets out for a rematch against the Top Three and Bachira. Will the “monster” that fuels Isagi's ego be enough to take down the prodigy striker Rin Itoshi?!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol8"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol8" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol8_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=1ebddc8b537cc1a45bf15d96ec1e37f66a60a3e3f78ed1f433ebd04eace461a1"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 8&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/f43a578ec2dba2f0cdf1cee1675340e6abf7f82b.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2b287223f1118d55ff3cfae8d44e7f35"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The newly formed team of Isagi, Nagi, and Barou head to their next rival battle, where they face Kunigami, Chigiri, and Reo. Isagi knows their victory will depend on the team's ability to form a ""chemical reaction"" with their play styles. Isagi and Nagi have a fluid synergy, but Barou seems to be chafing against his new teammates... Who will emerge victorious from the battle of egos?!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt30"&gt;Pay $30 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol7"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol7" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol7_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=da505eda83745f76e1f8d157db7f1a3c7e9bb6cfd93f23392d7c7790db36bcfd"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/9087ad425a8341a96c5438b3b21ed0e045b59d8d.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=9b9fb056f5c558e897c6b3480bc2f175"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Despite their best efforts, Nagi and company were unable to stop Otoya and Karasu from breaking loose and tying up the score with a last-minute combo play. Even worse Nagi finds his passion flagging without Isagi there to fire him up. That’s when Nagi proposes a radical new strategy to his teammates: forget what they have to do and focus on what they want to do. Can they combine their egoistic dreams into one final, winning push?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol6"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_episodenagi_vol6" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_episodenagi_vol6_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=8ec96d4913dfcf38b1d0f785ac696250aec60bc010746bc1e6a5385b5d72852d"&gt;Blue Lock: Episode Nagi Vol. 6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/55f526c99d4ec53080cc6cb693b9138b7413babe.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=3cd2bf8bafa8c39ed39e285f156682be"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;As the curtain rose on the final rivalry battle of the Second Selection, Nagi suddenly found himself believing in his own skills for the first time. With one goal in the bag, he now sets out to confirm whether Reo was right about him being a prodigy. Nagi's team will need to find a way to thwart Otoya and Karasu's cool and calculating teamwork if they hope to seal the deal. They may not have the brains…but they do have the imagination!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol38"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol38" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol38_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=c7d3b3399cf67a78118577249db6442514114a39ee70f430c93620052c5c3a54"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 38&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/2bc53361cf3ac7cc17ddcc20357affbf8d97d16e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=70b8c11a565934d2fd662adf988d84a6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The U-20 World Cup match against France begins with a shocking goal by Charles only moments into the game. As Isagi and the others plot their counterattack, they’re stopped at every turn by France’s second-best player, Hugo. With Hugo’s provocations shaking the very foundations of Blue Lock, the team must either find a way to adapt or be utterly destroyed!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol37"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol37" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol37_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=05fa180a8fe40ea3de5889febd5c868ac64875c80716bd6b738423ad993dc9e9"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 37&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/e67012302be0e8355e162c511291091f3fd5bf8e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=d7ab7aa44c7ab247eaae900fa56f610a"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Only fifteen minutes remain in the First match of the U-20 World Cup. Japan is Far ahead with three points, but neither side is ready to call it a day. Team Blue Lock is determined to keep Nigeria goalless, while Nigeria is fired up by Isagi's challenge to come and surpass him. Even as this drama is unfolding on the field, Buratsuta is kicking off his ""Side B"" project behind the scenes…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol36"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol36" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol36_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=3aa1f7d4aac9edd9efede9b2b8620cedebde74a7f9b481f138149aa83e8c2ef0"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 36&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/eabc8a0be704f1fd5faefce7897fbbbef05befb7.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=e8a64c2fc7a8ec67623021979b5bbd5a"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The U-20 World Cup has finally begun! Blue Lock Japan's first match is against the kings of African soccer, Nigeria. From the moment of kick off, the match becomes a fearsome battle of non-stop attacks. As Isagi and the others display the results of their special training, the team of egotists competes with each other to see who can shine the brightest!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol35"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol35" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol35_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=988f350912237a781106bf49b0da7491068dd4b9915b092788da816c7c391ec4"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 35&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/66745ceedb48931da50cd00bc3f95af8066ac708.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=6b3debe02e2c17d5ca0cf0afdcfa41f3"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The U-20 World Cup is about to begin, and the egotist warriors are engaged in their own personalized special training. Meanwhile, as Nagi feels stuck in time and unable to forget the fire he found, he comes face to face with a man offering him a fateful choice… As this vortex of wills swirls ever more fiercely, the curtain rises on a U-20 World Cup sure to shake the foundations of Japanese soccer!!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol34"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol34" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol34_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=e656a38148619b17f87a6c307b098ae3fd1bbe196021a6eda4793f6d0754e69a"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 34&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/3ee3919701781f2f13d2746d42062863f9e50e25.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=3e99f48cc83c683fe57bae1c010a4e16"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thanks to Isagi's game-ending goal, Germany clinched victory in the Neo-Egoist League. Will this Finally be enough to earn Isagi the top spot in the salary rankings? Meanwhile, Ego announces which players will be leaving Blue Lock, and the list includes one name nobody expected … With the start of the U-20 World Cup, the time has now come for Blue Lock to devour the world. The hottest place in the world for soccer is here!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol33"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol33" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol33_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=dcf36f388398e978b695992617687a74087dc4bbf8072937a8074dda16bb9e34"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 33&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6288ea2ad4b2493818df52b7552f5dfd8ec9bed9.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=9c2aa6dac73123169441948235eb79d4"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Isagi and Kaiser teamed up to snag the last goal, pushing the entire Bastard Munchen squad into overdrive. Not to be outdone, PXG responded with no less fierce offensive and defensive teamwork. In the midst of this heated battle, Ness feels himself being left behind by Kaiser and Frantically searches for a way forward. As the players race toward an unreadable climax, who will be the champion of the Neo-Egoist League?!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol32"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol32" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol32_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=49febaae6178cfd8f1064a0903bcf8dc326934c3c1bfdd954470824531daf509"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 32&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/d2312011b8e9c45399745767054fe5430c1f52ae.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=8c3e42e4479f4d442f253b8a15471fe6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the final match between Germany and France, Rin Itoshi had another awakening and tied the score with an incredible goal. Sensing the rapid change unfolding on the field, Loki decides to enter the fray, prompting Noa to join in as well. With both masters in play, Isagi must analyze a way to break out of this deadlock and score… The end draws near, and the world-changing goal is just around the corner!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol31"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol31" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol31_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=866ef92f927767be69e047738c273dfc89292771958194da95ac1a9ad2293b3d"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 31&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/97e04cb3ffae64ce6054da098da583dccaf85115.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=52b240acddf0fb6ee100e82005e75f44"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;After stripping away all pretense and remaking himself on the pitch, Kaiser unleashed the new-and-improved Kaiser Impact Magnus to bring the score to 2-1. Key to his success was his discovery that he works best under ""constraints,"" with Isagi's meteoric rise providing the challenge he needed to evolve. But Rin's just as hungry for a goal, and with both Kaiser and Isagi now closing in on his throne, the time might be ripe for an awakening…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol30"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol30" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol30_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=1ce8f7f626bd54676a0da50f85acb453932d205465138de1afe1e7f780d588ac"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 30&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/cdf5978da21d54f7ecf25007b16fe9c6beb2ed30.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=6c6448168742916e1ad9706d6d7f4112"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the first half of the PXG versus Bastard München match, Isagi combined his left- and right-leg skills into a devastating new weapon, the two-gun direct volley. With Isagi now knocking on the top spot in the rankings, Kaiser sees his chance for revenge and redemption slipping away. But sometimes winning means tossing aside,everything you care about-glory, status, pride-until the only thing left…is the “zero” at the root of it all.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol29"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol29" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol29_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=7e36aab7a6527917a9990dfec58a88cbea49f188a9aee7ee2617332e7fccba18"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 29&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/cd347e38c9a16bfee0b04b5c2656f9079ec4e311.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=da8a03f43d99b125494164a742e52ac5"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The final match of the Neo Egoist League finally kicks off! Amid the fierce battle, Loki's Team France unveils their new attack featuring Shidou and Charles. On the other side, Germany's egotists are close to an awakening as they throw themselves into the attack. And as Isagi is targeted by Kaiser and Rin, he figures out how to display his “ultimate”... Can he break through his fierce enemies and score a goal?!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol28"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol28" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol28_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=5eace3b0020940c0f40fe6e6fef713d755a9fcc9a9aa32147b687007b75ea06e"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 28&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/567c6f2bf014eee389085f270e21f509b0e0377e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=dcf136c45d007bbaf91aff01309d02cc"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Having reignited his passion for soccer, Hiori delivered Isagi a pinpoint pass that ended in the winning goal against Ubers. Isagi's stunning performance helps him shoot up to second place in the rankings but he still comes up short against the top-ranked player, Rin Itoshi. As the Neo-Egoist League nears its dramatic final day, each player must look inward and discover what he hungers for…but will mere hunger be enough?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol27"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol27" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol27_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=cb1dfccc374a538678a5ddc6c83cca8f1a247f201c7adeaad5f771830eeb486f"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 27&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/31488be2996371ba649be020fe15da93f9b6117d.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=41cd3fddff6e97c5bf0ab5e4f395ec62"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;After seemingly rejecting Snuffy's strategy and going rogue, “King” Barou tied up the game with a crazy double nutmeg. Isagi seethes at being outplayed yet again, but with Yo Hiori's entry into the match, he now has a new piece to help him turn the tide. As a furious battle unfolds on the pitch, Hiori grapples with his complicated feelings toward soccer and his place in Blue Lock. A part of him may be ready to call it quits, but another hungers for something more…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol26"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol26" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol26_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=36942b09e157262b3bf5da65fc69a891ce2efebb7bee725957be479c94141a5f"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 26&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6e29a760573e8863a7bcab9bfc923db17978a0c2.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=7b6f69fb509a6b9d70fe25857f5c53e7"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Isagi was riding high after scoring against Ubers, but then Kaiser sent an explosive shot crashing against the net. With Isagi and Kaiser now tied on goals and Bastard München up two to one against Ubers, Germany's and Italy's masters decide to join the fray. Snuffy deploys his players with the precision of a chess master, and Bastard München soon begins to buckle under Ubers' counterattack. Can Isagi find someone to be their “sacrificial pawn” and stop Italy's advance?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol25"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol25" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol25_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=408e91202e7c66a85325a3fec27d4eca44575ed32dd4e3794023681974237d37"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 25&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/479f717bc2ade42be0d6de6516f7a78b9f146ab6.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=ef7b82b2b7be3c2eff6b4eb1b2e2e7f5"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Isagi has finally scored his own goal in the Neo-Egoist League, courtesy of his newly unveiled “side weapon,” the lefty direct shot. Yet this is no time to get complacent. Italy's master, Snuffy, immediately brings his tactical genius to bear in Ubers' counterattack, but Barou chafes against his philosophy of soccer as “work.” Meanwhile, Niko, Kaiser, and Aiku all turn their own specialized weapons on Isagi as they seek to knock him down a peg. Ready, set…duel!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol24"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol24" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol24_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=692b6e00b73a41a43006985015cc75b9ab9f95cfd86771711e9e676f2b716129"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 24&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/60c82301d8f83b0448ce753f0ef56a8d7b0dc33e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=744df493797823c0c4c573f377efb0c3"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bastard München bounced back against Manshine City, with Yukimiya getting an assist from Isagi to clinch the winning goal. After Isagi collapses from overexertion, Noel Noa brings him up to speed on the new rankings, which show “King” Barou of Italy's Ubers claiming the top spot. With Bastard München facing Ubers in the next match, this will surely be their toughest battle yet. Can lsagi put his new “100 percent meta vision” into practice and dethrone the king??&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol23"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol23" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol23_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=ecb238a8924f6560ec34e33a6feb01aeb20dd2a56415c53b1bbc2828a70a651f"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 23&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/d9e1a1b558bb1144b06f524f633a216df36da369.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=c9ecc03237bd915c5069b951d74b72d7"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Just when it looked like Chris Prince was about to give England the lead, Isagi slid in and stopped the ball a hair's breadth from the goal. Fired up by the roaring crowd, Isagi now prepares a furious counterattack…only for his teammate Yukimiya to steal the ball and all his momentum. Isagi may be desperate to score in the final minutes, but Yukimiya is racing against an even more daunting countdown: his failing eyesight. Can he keep his story going, or will this be the final chapter?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol22"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol22" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol22_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=6d4f5c5fa35bee27c5f47b9b1d01710fbe3796393e6148d9664d8f9fcef7e19d"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 22&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/25baa602db552e78d4acba716c15e883c1f31ff2.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5fa729251d85bc87e38f3a346e8105e7"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manshine City's early lead evaporated following two goals from Kaiser and Kunigami. Meanwhile, Isagi discovered a new “golden formula” by combining Kaiser's “meta vision” with his direct shots. The question is, can he translate that into his own goal and finally get revenge on Kaiser? On the other side of the pitch, Nagi approaches Reo with an unexpected proposition. Can the on-again, off-again friends join forces to defeat Isagi and Bastard München?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol21"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol21" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol21_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=c8b17d08c8dc0936dddc3a9b56588316b40d2d9b27c449f24e1ad4a177fedf41"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 21&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/1999612ab93af2dce62c3c65711bcae6aa9161e0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5722eaf92f1c9da257bb93fd56973414"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Bastard München versus Manshine City match opened with a tremendous goal from Chigiri, who's leveled up his game with a little help from Chris Prince. As Bastard München launches a counterattack, Isagi finds some much-needed backup in Kurona. However, the specter of his teammate Kaiser is always there to shut him out from any scoring opportunities. Can he find the missing piece and finally escape the tyrant's shadow?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol20"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol20" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol20_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=3be8700635376cfa7dc815224f56dfe564b6d5b4ec61081e898b80749b4154f8"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 20&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/9f95755eda838968e43ab9cd398bec1203257821.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=cca2e8bb8a04db2722c582967366380e"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Despite failing to score against FC Barcha, Isagi gave Kunigami a crucial assist and helped spur Bastard München to victory. Even as the dust settles on the match, Ego reveals a shocking twist that will upend the Neo-Egoist League and bring the competition to a fever pitch. Now Bastard München prepares to take on its next opponent, Manshine City, in a contest of rationality versus speed and physicality. Which philosophy will come out on top?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol19"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol19" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol19_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=51d5d550d75287f4d830d4ec2a7186ffbcdb52873d35af52aa370e47de4e0ab5"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/47ee47532a6445fcd2120383056805be42f96358.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=124886700303caa351589a055a573a82"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unable to best Michael Kaiser during training, Isagi was relegated to the bench for Bastard München's first match against FC Barcha. Despite his frustration, Isagi resolves to analyze every second of the match so he can draw level with the evolved Bachira and Kunigami. But wait... Noel Noa's coming onto the field?! What follows is a truly epic clash of soccer gods and monsters-one that might even bring Isagi off the bench...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol18"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol18" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol18_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=c58b210f0ea31b8d14841f00914362f374e4623babb4218a888840f7dff53e4c"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/c67161dba7af9925369078cead47aa2fd175bef9.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5aced9730536ef4868001afb7c4b0034"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Still basking in the glow of victory against the U-20 Japan team, the Blue Lock Eleven enjoy some well-earned downtime in Shibuya. But their rest proves short-lived, as Ego soon calls everyone together to reveal the details of Phase Two. In this next challenge, the strikers will have the opportunity to train with professional U-20 players from the biggest European leagues. The stakes are higher and the rivalries ever fiercer… Let Phase Two begin!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="bluelock_vol17"&gt;&lt;a id="bluelock_vol17" href="https://cdn.humble.com/humblebundle/ops/pdfs/bluelock_vol17_preview.pdf?t=st=1794050893~exp=1794137293~hmac=a13107a202e4589743985360a1b9fcdf8ed997cc418141a040f1adcc245fd056"&gt;Blue Lock Vol. 17&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/b0e936884e9cfdd79a083df12adb106092257885.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=0ee368e5c8932a5cf006de3124e8bd27"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;As they entered the second half of the Blue Lock Eleven versus U-20 Japan match, Isagi, Rin, and Barou each vied to be the first to reach a flow state. The ensuing clash of egos kicked up the level of play and brought them even with the U-20 Japan team. Now, with the clock winding down and everything on the line, Bachira emerges as Isagi's final puzzle piece. Can they stave off the U-20 counterattack and claw their way to victory?!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
