ady Projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="middleeastern_ashesofthebazaar"&gt;&lt;a id="middleeastern_ashesofthebazaar" href="https://youtu.be/ziRfFr8Dcsw"&gt;Middle Eastern - Ashes of the Bazaar&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ashes of Bazaar Environment with 101 Unique Meshes. Including all showcased and high-quality assets. With a good level of detail and optimized for Game Ready Projects. If you want to populate your game environments or any kind of Virtual Production levels here is the pack that you get and use to get high-quality visuals and well-optimized assets. DISCLAIMER: Nanite/Lumen Enabled This product supports Lumen for Unreal Engine 5.5.4 Features: 105 Unique Meshes Attention to Detail / AAA Quality Controllable parameters in Material Instances High-Quality Assets Game ready/Optimized Unique Concepts of Assets High Attention to Details Material Variations For Some Assets Texture Sizes: 4096 2048 Texture Size: 4096 for some assets like tents, 2048 for props and some architectural meshes Collision: Yes LODs: LOD0 Number of Meshes: 101 Number of Materials and Material Instances: 93 Number of Textures: 193 Supported Development Platforms: All Platforms Supported Development Versions: Unreal Engine 5.5.4+&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="forgottenechoesenvironment"&gt;&lt;a id="forgottenechoesenvironment" href="https://youtu.be/DN3L35XyVYE"&gt;Forgotten Echoes Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Forgotten Echoes Environment with 140 Unique Meshes. Including all showcased assets, and high-quality assets. With a good level of detail and optimized for Game Ready Projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="frozenharborfortress"&gt;&lt;a id="frozenharborfortress" href="https://youtu.be/uX4cyjw9IsA"&gt;Frozen Harbor Fortress&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Environment created by Leo Gosselet, 1st Place Winner of the 3D Environment Art category in the Veiled Realms Art Challenge Modular Nordic Architecture: Modular walls, stone arches, and windmills. Atmospheric Winter Environment: Snowy harbor aesthetics, fog, wrecks, and icicles. Advanced Master Materials: Customizable snow, ice overlay, and weathering parameters. Nanite &amp;amp; Lumen Support: High-poly optimization and dynamic global illumination. AAA Cinematic Quality: Optimized LOD transitions and high-resolution textures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="qaagent_crashreportingandaidebugging"&gt;&lt;a id="qaagent_crashreportingandaidebugging" href="https://youtu.be/AAElNhCe4WI"&gt;QA Agent: Crash Reporting &amp; AI Debugging&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;QA Agent: Crash Reporting &amp;amp; AI Debugging Watch The Showcase / Trailer Crash and Bug Reporting for Unreal Engine Teams Please note that the product is still in beta. Documentation Included Please click here to access the documentation package, which includes a README, Quick Start Guide, User Guide, Installation Guide, FAQ, Technical Specifications, and Product Description. QA Agent helps Unreal Engine teams turn crashes and bug reports into actionable information without requiring a dedicated QA department. Key Features Readable Crash Reports Capture symbolicated callstacks with function names, source files, and line numbers. When available, QA Agent also captures Blueprint execution context and variable values to help developers identify the cause of a crash. In-Game Bug Reporting Testers can press F8 to submit a bug report directly from the game. Reports can include a screenshot, player position, device information, performance metrics, session duration, and recent log lines. Discord Integration Send reports directly to a Discord forum channel. Similar crashes are grouped into threads, with repeat counts, report ownership, and resolution status to help teams manage bugs efficiently. AI-Assisted Crash Analysis Optionally analyze new crash reports to identify likely causes and suggest potential fixes. Repeated reports do not trigger the same analysis again, helping keep processing costs predictable. Developer-Reviewed Fix Suggestions Use the local fix panel to generate source-code patches and review their differences before approval. QA Agent does not automatically rewrite Blueprints; instead, it helps developers locate the relevant Blueprint nodes when the required context is available. Requirements Unreal Engine 5.5–5.8 Windows 64-bit Node.js 24 or newer for the server A Discord server with a forum channel and a configured bot An Anthropic API key for optional AI analysis Privacy and Data Handling The server runs on a machine controlled by your team. Discord and AI credentials remain in the server configuration and are not embedded in game builds. Optional AI features send relevant report data and, when configured, selected source-code snippets to Anthropic. QA Agent filters recognized sensitive patterns in shared logs, but this filtering is not guaranteed anonymization. Review the documentation before enabling source-code analysis or deploying the plugin in a shipping build.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="projectoptimizationtoolkitpotperformanceoptimizationassetcleaner"&gt;&lt;a id="projectoptimizationtoolkitpotperformanceoptimizationassetcleaner" href="https://youtu.be/WMz0THALIXg"&gt;Project Optimization Toolkit POT (Performance Optimization, Asset Cleaner )&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Project Optimization Toolkit (POT) is a comprehensive editor extension for Unreal Engine 5 published by Leartes Studios. It is engineered to help development teams keep their projects clean, lean, and structurally sound by combining three powerful diagnostic utilities into a single plugin: a Health Dashboard, an Asset Cleaner, and a Dependency Visualizer. Showcase / Trailer Video: https://youtu.be/WMz0THALIXg Built specifically for day-to-day production environments, POT operates entirely locally inside the editor without requiring external services or third-party accounts. Its background scans run smoothly without blocking user workflows, and any heavy processing or deletion tasks are handled in safe, cancellable batches. Documentations and Guides DISCLAIMER: For a huge projects over 50gb system might get stuck and needs to wait a long time for the fixes. Key Features 1. Health Dashboard Project Health Scoring: Generates a real-time project health score from 0 to 100 along with an A–F letter grade, dynamically computed based on the severity of discovered issues and estimated wasted disk space. Nine Analysis Categories: Systematically inspects your project across nine specialized providers: project health, texture audit, mesh audit, duplicate detection, reference health, external files, unused assets, missing references, and indirect references. One-Click Automated Fixes: Offers direct, in-place corrections for various asset alignment errors, such as enabling Nanite on eligible meshes, adjusting Level of Detail (LOD) settings, repairing mipmap and texture compression settings, adding collisions, and resolving stale redirectors. Reversible Transactions: All automated fixes are applied as editor transactions, allowing developers to immediately revert any unexpected changes using standard Ctrl+Z operations. 2. Asset Cleaner Comprehensive Waste Detection: Automatically identifies and isolates unused assets, duplicate files, empty folders, non-asset external files, corrupted disk assets, and obsolete redirectors. Accurate Reachability Analysis: By default, the cleaner uses an Accurate detection mode that starts at explicitly active roots (maps, primary assets, editor utilities, and code/config references) and maps the dependency chain outward. This enables it to flag entire dead branches of assets that are only referenced by other unused assets. Content-Aware Duplicate Matching: Features a deep structural matching pass that evaluates base level-of-detail geometry for static meshes and parameter arrays for material instances, successfully grouping identical files even if they differ byte-for-byte on disk. Safe Deletion Safeguards: Includes protective measures such as explicit counts and size summaries, mandatory verification prompts, and designated warnings for assets tied to indirect code or config references. Continuous Integration (CI) Commandlet: Ships with a dedicated headless commandlet (-run=POTCleaner) to automate scanning and scheduled cleanup pipelines on remote build machines. 3. Dependency Visualizer Interactive Graphing: Renders reference structures as node-and-edge graphs where users can interactively expand or collapse pathways to inspect asset connections. Eight Layout Modes: Provides eight distinct layout configurations (such as hierarchical flow, radial/force-directed clusters, or compact grids) that can be swapped instantly without rebuilding the graph. Circular Dependency Detection: Runs real-time cycle tracking to highlight looping references, allowing teams to break structural loops before they cause load-order or cooking failures. Snapshot Comparison: Captures graph states at specific intervals, providing side-by-side analysis to track exact reference changes, additions, or deletions across a project's history or during refactoring phases. Custom Customization &amp;amp; Tooling: Supports manual annotations, viewpoint bookmarking, reusable configurations, and graph exporting into thirteen external data or vector formats. It also exposes a fully Blueprint-callable API to drive custom automated tools. Technical Specifications &amp;amp; Requirements Unreal Engine Compatibility: Supports Unreal Engine versions 5.1 through 5.8. Supported Platform: Windows 64-bit (Editor-only plugin; it does not add overhead to packaged game builds). Project Frameworks: Fully operational with both Blueprint-only and native C++ projects. Engine Dependencies: Relies on Unreal’s built-in Asset Manager Editor plugin, which POT enables automatically upon initialization. Source Control Integration: Deletion routines funnel seamlessly into Unreal's standard asset disposal paths, interfacing natively with source control providers like Perforce or Git.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="stylizedeasternprovinceenvironment"&gt;&lt;a id="stylizedeasternprovinceenvironment" href="https://youtu.be/x3xgC4yoyk4"&gt;Stylized Eastern Province Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stylized Eastern Province with 141 Assets. There are many different types of Assets to help you create or polish your Environments. All Assets made with unique concepts and Showcased Example levels are also included in the Project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="underwaterartdecohotelenvironment"&gt;&lt;a id="underwaterartdecohotelenvironment" href="https://youtu.be/zcNokvCb5mY"&gt;Underwater Art Deco Hotel Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Underwater Art Deco Hotel Environment with over 250 unique meshes. Dive into a luxurious, retro-futuristic world beneath the waves. This comprehensive modular asset pack seamlessly blends the opulence of classic 1920s Art Deco architecture with a breathtaking deep-sea setting, allowing you to build an unforgettable submarine paradise. Includes Showcased Preassembled Scene Ideal for first-person adventures, sci-fi exploration games, and stylized cinematic projects. Construct sprawling deep-sea resorts featuring a grand hotel lobby centered around a golden mermaid fountain, soaring brass columns, and a massive glass dome ceiling peering directly into the marine depths. Detail your levels with high-end bar lounges, luxury living areas, and endless hotel hallways with geometric brass-inlay doors. The pack also features beautiful, arched stained-glass corridors and curved observation tunnels for panoramic views of coral reefs and aquatic life. The environment is enriched with dense, era-specific storytelling props, including checkerboard marble flooring, plush velvet seating, geometric wall sconces, retro appliances, indoor palm trees, and translucent green glass partitions. The pack comes complete with a pre-assembled showcase scene, utilizing lighting with Lumen to demonstrate how the shimmering, bioluminescent green tones of the ocean filter through the glass to cast beautiful reflections across polished marble and metallic surfaces. Lumen enabled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="containerportenvironment"&gt;&lt;a id="containerportenvironment" href="https://youtu.be/eMGWieCLT6o"&gt;Container Port Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Container Port Environment with 522 Unique Meshes. Including all showcased assets, and high-quality assets. With a good level of detail and optimized for Game Ready Projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="cyberpunkapartment"&gt;&lt;a id="cyberpunkapartment" href="https://youtu.be/zmoyEjQGRBM"&gt;Cyberpunk Apartment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cyberpunk / Sci Fi / Futuristic Apartment Interior, includes 132 unique assets and 7 very useful blueprints which you can check out in the tutorial video, the apartment is a hacker's flat who lives in a Cyberpunk world and spends most of his time in his messy flat to hack / challenge AI forces.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="fantasygothiccastle"&gt;&lt;a id="fantasygothiccastle" href="https://youtu.be/u02EHPLs2Qs"&gt;Fantasy Gothic Castle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fantasy Gothic Castle Environment with 83 Unique Meshes. Including all showcased assets, and high-quality assets. With a good level of detail and optimized for Game Ready Projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="medievaltavern_leartes"&gt;&lt;a id="medievaltavern_leartes" href="https://youtu.be/Y6qOhfifA7w"&gt;Medieval Tavern&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Medieval Tavern Environment with 123 Unique Meshes. Including all showcased assets, high-quality assets. With a good level of detail and optimized for Game Ready Projects. The Medieval Tavern has two light sublevel with lev