      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/9808267f37c4ce04969dfbf7f2f90550777199d6.png?auto=compress,format&amp;h=340&amp;w=1200&amp;s=da33bb8a6ad02d7a24769cc6986ef4bb"&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/b7d537983d7450346c2b0f5b31e04d6ef7ac1048.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=crop&amp;h=600&amp;w=1200&amp;s=1e19101eae6cef4f25bd03482c48aa94"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Create your own video games!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Become a game dev mastermind when you harness the power of Godot, Unreal Engine, and Unity! Learn how to create your own open-world survival game from the ground up with fresh foraging tactics, build a silky-smooth stealth game with compelling combat mechanics, get tactical with a new take on the RTS genre, build an action-adventure game, and so much more with this curated bundle of approachable learning courses. Harness the power of game creation to bring your dream game to life, all for a price you choose. Unlock the very best from Zenva and help support Alzheimer's Research UK with your purchase.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#0"&gt;Pay $5 to unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#exploreaudioforgodot4games"&gt;Explore Audio for Godot 4 Games&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#explorecinematiccutscenesforunitygames"&gt;Explore Cinematic Cutscenes for Unity Games&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bt15"&gt;Pay $15 or more to also unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildawalkingsimulatorwithgodot4"&gt;Build a Walking Simulator with Godot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#first-personexplorationgameinunrealengine2026edition"&gt;First-Person Exploration Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bt25"&gt;Pay $25 or more to also unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#createanopenworldsurvivalgameingodot4"&gt;Create an Open World Survival Game in Godot 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#introtogodot4gamedevelopment2025edition"&gt;Intro to Godot 4 Game Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#godot4mini-projects2025edition"&gt;Godot 4 Mini-Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildacompletepuzzlegamewithgodotandc"&gt;Build a Complete Puzzle Game with Godot and C#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#createahorrorgameingodot4"&gt;Create a Horror Game in Godot 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#coincollectorgame-godotmobileprojects"&gt;Coin Collector Game - Godot Mobile Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#createamicroturn-basedrpgingodot2025edition"&gt;Create a Micro Turn-Based RPG in Godot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#towerdefensegameingodot_unit1_basegame"&gt;Tower Defense Game in Godot - Unit 1 - Base Game&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildacompletestealthgamewithunrealengine"&gt;Build a Complete Stealth Game with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildanrtsgamewithunrealengine"&gt;Build an RTS Game with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#introtounrealenginegamedevelopment2025edition"&gt;Intro to Unreal Engine Game Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#unrealenginemini-projects2025edition"&gt;Unreal Engine Mini-Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildatowerdefensegameinunrealengine"&gt;Build a Tower Defense Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#developaclassicshootemupwithunrealengine"&gt;Develop a Classic Shoot 'em up with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#createaracinggameinunrealengine"&gt;Create a Racing Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#makeafully-fledged3dplatformerwithunrealengine"&gt;Make a Fully-Fledged 3D Platformer with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#makeamini-survivalgameinunrealengine"&gt;Make a Mini-Survival Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#developacity-buildinggamewithunity"&gt;Develop a City-Building Game with Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildanarcadekartracinggameinunity"&gt;Build an Arcade Kart Racing Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#introtogamedevelopmentwithunity2025edition"&gt;Intro to Game Development with Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#unitymini-projects_cfundamentals"&gt;Unity Mini-Projects - C# Fundamentals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#crafta2didleclickergameinunity"&gt;Craft a 2D Idle Clicker Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#buildamobileroadcrossinggameinunity"&gt;Build a Mobile Road Crossing Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#constructafirstpersonshooterinunity"&gt;Construct a First Person Shooter in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#createaretrolocalmultiplayergameinunity"&gt;Create a Retro Local Multiplayer Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#createa3dturn-basedrpginunity"&gt;Create a 3D Turn-Based RPG in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 id="0"&gt;Pay $5 to unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="exploreaudioforgodot4games"&gt;&lt;a id="exploreaudioforgodot4games" href="https://youtu.be/vT_km5EOGts"&gt;Explore Audio for Godot 4 Games&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Implement audio for your Godot games!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Audio is an important facet of many game genres for creating atmosphere, immersion, and gameplay feedback. In this course, you'll dive into various ways you can implement audio in Godot as well as how to set up volume control settings for players. These skills will give you the foundations to add audio to any Godot game and enhance the overall game feel.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add general background music&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement footsteps for player movement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create the Doppler effect&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up reverb zones&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Separate audio tracks with buses&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop in-game volume controls&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="explorecinematiccutscenesforunitygames"&gt;&lt;a id="explorecinematiccutscenesforunitygames" href="https://youtu.be/tfNDgg9LSWU"&gt;Explore Cinematic Cutscenes for Unity Games&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enhance your game projects by learning to create cinematic cutscenes!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Utilizing Cinemachine and the Unity Timeline, you'll develop skills for creating simple 3D animations and dynamic camera shots. You'll master all these while building an exciting police car chase cutscene with multiple shots, post-processing effects, and more. Regardless of the type of game you're making, these abilities will give you the knowledge you need to craft engaging cutscenes, enhance your stories, and keep your players interested.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up projects for cutscenes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use position and rotation for 3D animation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Adjust lighting and post-processing aesthetics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create a variety of Cinemachine camera shots&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement a dolly camera tracking shot&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control animations and shots with the Unity Timeline&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt15"&gt;Pay $15 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildawalkingsimulatorwithgodot4"&gt;&lt;a id="buildawalkingsimulatorwithgodot4" href="https://youtu.be/n0ctopwKaQE"&gt;Build a Walking Simulator with Godot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create an atmospheric walking simulator with Godot!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Walking simulators make exploring and interacting with a game world the central experience. In this course, you'll follow step-by-step guidance to build a complete walking simulator in Godot, bringing an interactive forest setting to life from a first-person perspective. With these skills, you can move on to developing an adventure, mystery, or puzzle game using your project as a foundation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build 3D environments with imported assets&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Shape atmosphere with lighting and fog&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Script first-person movement and camera controls&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create object interaction prompts and actions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement footsteps that accompany player movement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add ambient sound and interaction feedback&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="first-personexplorationgameinunrealengine2026edition"&gt;&lt;a id="first-personexplorationgameinunrealengine2026edition" href="https://youtu.be/5qPwFmXwG8Y"&gt;First-Person Exploration Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build a fully-fledged first-person exploration game using Unreal Engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;First-person exploration games captivate players by immersing them in interactive worlds, where storytelling and discovery are at the core of the experience. In this course, you’ll develop a modular first-person exploration game inside Unreal Engine, mastering key systems that empower you to craft compelling puzzles, environments, and interactive stories. By the end, you’ll possess reusable tools and in-depth techniques to bring a wide range of first-person games to life.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up a first-person controller&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop versatile interaction systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create dynamic door and object logic&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Display info boxes for storytelling&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement Blueprints for rapid iteration&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Integrate assets for immersive worlds&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt25"&gt;Pay $25 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="createanopenworldsurvivalgameingodot4"&gt;&lt;a id="createanopenworldsurvivalgameingodot4" href="https://youtu.be/LPn-vYup36Y"&gt;Create an Open World Survival Game in Godot 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Develop an open-world survival game in Godot 4!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open worlds are a popular feature for survival games and can add tons of value for replayability. In this course, you'll discover techniques for combining modular systems for players, enemies, items, and procedural generation to craft a complex open-world game ready for your customizations. These skills will allow you to work with open worlds for different genres as well as understand the fundamental construction for survival mechanics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Generate terrain&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement enemy spawn points&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Tweak environments for different visuals&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add and modify collectible resources&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Customize weapons and items&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Make complex games with simple systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="introtogodot4gamedevelopment2025edition"&gt;&lt;a id="introtogodot4gamedevelopment2025edition" href="https://youtu.be/xfJHHhLC_QE"&gt;Intro to Godot 4 Game Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Start your game development journey with Godot - the powerful, open-source game engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Godot is a versatile tool for 2D and 3D game development, combining beginner-friendly workflows with powerful professional features.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this course, you'll explore the essential features of Godot by gaining hands-on experience in core development tools, 2D design, 3D environments, and coding gameplay behaviors with GDScript from start to finish.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dive in and gain the foundations you'll need to make RPGs, survival games, and more with Godot!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Navigate the Godot editor&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Utilize core editing tools&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Understand Nodes and Scenes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with 2D &amp;amp; 3D assets&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Script gameplay behaviors with GDScript&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop a basic interactive game&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="godot4mini-projects2025edition"&gt;&lt;a id="godot4mini-projects2025edition" href="https://youtu.be/gakrT33ByrY"&gt;Godot 4 Mini-Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn essential game development tools through engaging Godot mini-projects!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Godot is a leading open-source game engine known for its flexibility in creating both 2D and 3D games. In this course, you'll create four practical mini-projects designed to solidify your grasp on crucial game mechanics and programming concepts. From mouse input handling to 2D physics systems and collision detection, these hands-on projects will form the foundation needed to build more complex, complete games in the future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement mouse-click-driven interactions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with Godot’s physics engine&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Detect collisions and handle responses&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use loops to automate complex systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create dynamic UI for player interaction&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Communicate between scripts&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildacompletepuzzlegamewithgodotandc"&gt;&lt;a id="buildacompletepuzzlegamewithgodotandc" href="https://youtu.be/i5h9VcyuqHY"&gt;Build a Complete Puzzle Game with Godot and C#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Explore number-based puzzle games for C# and Godot!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Puzzle games offer developers opportunities to explore simple but unique mechanics that require logical thinking from players. Through this course, you'll build your own version of a popular sliding tile number game while exploring how to develop with C# in Godot. These skills will allow you to unlock the world of puzzles for video games and begin discovering how to work with mechanics that have replayability in mind!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with grid systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage user input for puzzles&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement tile sliding mechanics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Merge tiles using math-based logic&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add animations and aesthetics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control scoring and game-over conditions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="createahorrorgameingodot4"&gt;&lt;a id="createahorrorgameingodot4" href="https://youtu.be/Ty_XEsdBF2s"&gt;Create a Horror Game in Godot 4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Make your own horror game in Godot 4!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Horror games are an extremely popular and beloved genre for both indie developers and AAA developers. Through this course, you'll explore how to build a horror game where the player collects chalices in a dark and spooky forest - all while learning how different systems like player movement and enemy AI work together. These skills will give you the foundations for not only building atmospheric horror games, but combining different systems to make a complete game project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Plan horror game designs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Craft atmospheric horror levels&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create moveable light systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement enemy AI behavior&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control game over conditions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Merge modular systems together&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="coincollectorgame-godotmobileprojects"&gt;&lt;a id="coincollectorgame-godotmobileprojects" href="https://youtu.be/HyIzC09Bd3k"&gt;Coin Collector Game - Godot Mobile Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master player movement for mobile games in Godot!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mobile games allow for a robust collection of inputs - including UI-based mechanics to mimic controllers, keyboards, and more.  Through this course, you'll build a time-based game where players must move around a 2D character with a keyboard-like interface to collect coins. These techniques will allow you to unlock different styles of player interactions for mobile games that can be adapted to the project's needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Craft 2D player movement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Accept "keyboard" inputs via UIs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with animations&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Spawn coins with increasing difficulty&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create time-based health reduction&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement particle systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="createamicroturn-basedrpgingodot2025edition"&gt;&lt;a id="createamicroturn-basedrpgingodot2025edition" href="https://youtu.be/xMrNK6JFgzM"&gt;Create a Micro Turn-Based RPG in Godot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Develop a micro turn-based RPG from start to finish using Godot!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turn-based RPGs are a cornerstone of game development, offering engaging mechanics based on strategic decision-making and rewarding gameplay loops. In this course, you'll build a visually engaging micro turn-based RPG in Godot where players face off against an AI opponent in tactical combat. These skills will enable you to tackle more advanced game projects, design fully-fledged RPG experiences, and refine your programming expertise in Godot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design a turn-based combat system&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create custom player and AI actions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement AI decision-making with variables&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Incorporate menus and game UI mechanics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add game feel with visual and audio polish&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Finalize a complete, playable project&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="towerdefensegameingodot_unit1_basegame"&gt;&lt;a id="towerdefensegameingodot_unit1_basegame" href="https://youtu.be/pHg8tiZxJxU"&gt;Tower Defense Game in Godot - Unit 1 - Base Game&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build a basic tower defense game in Godot!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tower defense games are renowned for their blend of action, strategy, and real-time decision-making. Through this course, you’ll construct the foundational systems of a tower defense game by programming enemy wave spawns, implementing a working tower with real targeting logic, developing bullet projectiles that track and damage enemies, and more. With these tower defense skills, you'll gain practical experience orchestrating interactions between scenes, signals, and groups in Godot - crucial skills for your future projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up wave enemy spawning&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create and program tower logic&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build bullet projectile mechanics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage dynamic stats&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Connect multiple scenes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use path following for enemies&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildacompletestealthgamewithunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="buildacompletestealthgamewithunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/jEVMwL6zCh4"&gt;Build a Complete Stealth Game with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create a fully-fledged 3D stealth game!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stealth gameplay is a cornerstone of modern action and adventure games, known for its tense strategies and immersive experiences. In this course, you'll build a complete stealth combat game in Unreal Engine, focusing on advanced enemy AI and dynamic stealth mechanics. With these skills, you'll be ready to specialize further in AI-driven design and tackle complex, real-world Unreal Engine projects in multiple genres.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design advanced enemy patrol systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement field of view mechanics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Integrate real-time sound detection&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build stealth and combat gameplay&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up character and enemy animations&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Construct game levels efficiently&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildanrtsgamewithunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="buildanrtsgamewithunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/c1baBELiWTY"&gt;Build an RTS Game with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master the fundamentals for RTS games in Unreal Engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Real-time strategy games combine the best of quick action and thought-provoking decisions - making them very popular. You'll explore core strategy mechanics including unit movement, basic combat, and more while building a small RTS project in Unreal. The techniques here will provide you with base mechanics that can be expanded or used in other strategy-style games!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Make playable units&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement simple combat&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Navigate with Nav Mesh&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide UI-feedback for input&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create RTS-appropriate cameras&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Improve level aesthetics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="introtounrealenginegamedevelopment2025edition"&gt;&lt;a id="introtounrealenginegamedevelopment2025edition" href="https://youtu.be/Jkm8K9PnQCg"&gt;Intro to Unreal Engine Game Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/bd171972da31ab2bbd23a175aa29068d66ec3c7b.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=627b10cb13fce82173fba91da8218647"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take your first step into Unreal Engine game development!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unreal Engine stands at the forefront of professional game development, powering everything from breakout indie hits to AAA blockbusters. Through this course, you’ll get hands-on with the Unreal Editor, master core mechanics, and build simple interactive examples using the Blueprints Visual Scripting system. With these skills, you'll unlock the foundation to craft immersive experiences and pursue more advanced Unreal Engine projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Navigate the Unreal Editor interface&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with actors and game objects&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up and modify level settings&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement realistic physics and lighting&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build gameplay with visual scripting&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Handle user interaction&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="unrealenginemini-projects2025edition"&gt;&lt;a id="unrealenginemini-projects2025edition" href="https://youtu.be/J2cgZ1psueY"&gt;Unreal Engine Mini-Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build four beginner-friendly Unreal Engine mini-games!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unreal Engine empowers creators to bring imaginative ideas to life, making it a cornerstone tool across all genres. In this course, you’ll build a set of four mini-projects exploring concepts like UIs, physics, and core programming tenets with real-world techniques that strengthen your grasp of the editor. The practical skills you gain will give you the confidence to take the next step in your Unreal Engine journey - whether you want to build RPGs, walking simulators, FPS games, or something else.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manipulate actor properties with scripting&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Utilize loops for mass object spawning&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build a game based on physics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop an interactive UI&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Connect player input to game mechanics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Apply Unreal best practices throughout&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildatowerdefensegameinunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="buildatowerdefensegameinunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/SjuCFNM_hZY"&gt;Build a Tower Defense Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create a complete tower defense game in Unreal Engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Tower defense games combine the best of strategy and creativity, making them a favorite among gamers. In this course, you’ll build a tower defense game while exploring character blueprints, animations, tile maps, and scalable game mechanics to develop a polished project that demonstrates the power of 2.5D gameplay. Mastering these skills will help you create modular tower defense games and expand into more advanced Unreal Engine projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create modular character blueprints&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up animations for all states&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design and decorate game levels&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement tower defense behavior and logic&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop a point system for strategic decisions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Combine 2D and 3D gameplay features&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="developaclassicshootemupwithunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="developaclassicshootemupwithunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/x4PjGp_WGsQ"&gt;Develop a Classic Shoot 'em up with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build a 3D arcade shooter from start to finish in Unreal Engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shoot ‘em ups are a timeless genre that has vastly influenced and shaped the landscape of action games. In this course, you’ll create your own shoot ‘em up in Unreal Engine while learning player controls, dynamic enemy spawning, collision systems, and interactive UI development. These practical, multifaceted skills can be used not just for building shoot 'em ups, but also for exploring new game genres with Unreal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build player movement and shooting logic&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design modular enemy-spawning systems&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement precise collision detection&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Integrate dynamic audio and SFX&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create visual polish with particles&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop a real-time game UI&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="createaracinggameinunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="createaracinggameinunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/Is4wgmFW9OQ"&gt;Create a Racing Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Make an arcade-style racing game in Unreal Engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Whether stylized or hyper-realistic, racing games are a popular genre due to their all-ages nature and easy-to-understand mechanics. In this course, you'll build a racing game while learning how to set up a car and a track that can manage laps. These techniques will give you the foundations to expand any sort of racing game and gain a deeper understanding of Blueprints techniques for vehicles in general.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement a race track environment&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add inputs suited to vehicles&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up a race car&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Detect racing progress&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control UIs and win conditions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Rig additional cars in Blender&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="makeafully-fledged3dplatformerwithunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="makeafully-fledged3dplatformerwithunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/oIwwn5bl2ek"&gt;Make a Fully-Fledged 3D Platformer with Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bring your own 3D platformer to life with Unreal Engine from start to finish!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3D platformers stand as classics of the gaming world, celebrated for their dynamic movement and multi-layered levels. Through this course, you’ll craft a fully-fledged 3D platformer from the ground up, building core features like animated players, collectibles, enemies, and seamless level progression. These skills will not only deepen your understanding of Unreal Engine, but give you the confidence to design original platforming experiences or evolve existing ones.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up a 3D player controller&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement movement, jumping, and animations&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create interconnected, multi-stage levels&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add collectibles that track player progress&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design enemy behavior and obstacles&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop in-game menus and UI&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="makeamini-survivalgameinunrealengine"&gt;&lt;a id="makeamini-survivalgameinunrealengine" href="https://youtu.be/fG-Jy6bghy0"&gt;Make a Mini-Survival Game in Unreal Engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create a mini-survival game using Unreal Engine!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Survival games are a staple of the industry with a unique ability to work in just about any setting. Through this course, you'll explore the most fundamental of survival game player mechanics, as well as how to set up environments for those players. These techniques will allow you to adapt any project for the survival game genre with universal concepts that can easily be expanded to suit your needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Craft terrain with Quixel&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Deal with user inputs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement player movement&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control player "needs"&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Construct companion UIs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Make day-night cycles&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="developacity-buildinggamewithunity"&gt;&lt;a id="developacity-buildinggamewithunity" href="https://youtu.be/ydwdyT6iyJA"&gt;Develop a City-Building Game with Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master strategy game mechanics for city-building games - all while creating your own from scratch! Step-by-step, you'll develop an isometric, turn-based city-builder where you can place various buildings and calculate the resources that they generate. You'll learn powerful systems to deal with resource management, and master other crucial game techniques that can be applied to many other types of strategy games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement a camera that can pan and zoom&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up a grid-based building placement system&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Detect mouse clicks in 3D space&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add different buildings that can be selected&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Calculate resources based on buildings constructed&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Relay game information with a UI&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildanarcadekartracinggameinunity"&gt;&lt;a id="buildanarcadekartracinggameinunity" href="https://youtu.be/U8MxxJ_GAhs"&gt;Build an Arcade Kart Racing Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enhance your Unity game development skills by learning to create a 3D kart racing game. You'll explore a variety of robust techniques for creating car movement with Unity's new Input System - including adding physics for believable car movement, tracking kart position for win conditions, and more. Besides racing mechanics, you'll also learn how to turn your project into a split-screen local multiplayer game, giving you the foundations you need to expand in whatever direction you want to for racing-style games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up kart racing inputs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build a simple racing track&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Adjust kart movement with physics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create systems for tracking race position&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control game flow with countdowns and win conditions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement split-screen multiplayer&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="introtogamedevelopmentwithunity2025edition"&gt;&lt;a id="introtogamedevelopmentwithunity2025edition" href="https://youtu.be/-bIsh3ozjSg"&gt;Intro to Game Development with Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Get started with Unity and unlock limitless game creation possibilities!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unity is the powerful, cross-platform engine behind some of the world’s most popular games and interactive experiences. Through this course, you’ll gain a solid foundation in Unity’s core systems, essential tools, and C# scripting - empowering you to bring your creative ideas to life across any genre or platform. By learning best practices and real-world workflows from start to finish, you’ll be ready to tackle your own projects with confidence and clarity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You'll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Install and set up Unity&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Navigate the Unity Editor interface&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage and manipulate GameObjects&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with lighting, physics, and more&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Write and integrate basic C# scripts&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create your first interactive project&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="unitymini-projects_cfundamentals"&gt;&lt;a id="unitymini-projects_cfundamentals" href="https://youtu.be/2239JlqoBLA"&gt;Unity Mini-Projects - C# Fundamentals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kickstart your Unity C# journey with playable mini-projects!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unity powers some of the world’s most popular games, and mastering its fundamentals opens doors to a wide array of creative opportunities in game development. In this course, you’ll build four mini-games - each focused on core topics like user interaction, physics, and collision detection. By completing these real-world projects, you’ll be ready to prototype your own interactive experiences, expand into more advanced Unity scripting, and create gameplay features with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design interactive Unity user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement responsive click-based mechanics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Apply for loops and optimize code&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with 3D textures and materials&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Harness Unity’s physics for gameplay&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Detect and handle collisions via code&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="crafta2didleclickergameinunity"&gt;&lt;a id="crafta2didleclickergameinunity" href="https://youtu.be/waniMSQuutA"&gt;Craft a 2D Idle Clicker Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master the Unity engine and build an incremental game - a popular genre for both desktops and mobile. You'll create a simple gold generating game based on clicks where the player can buy "clickers" to passively generate income. From implementing modern idle game mechanics to enhancing game "feel" with visual feedback, you'll develop strong foundations that can easily be expanded on for other idle games!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use Unity's UI system&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Damage enemies with clicks&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Provide gold on enemy death&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Randomize and cycle images&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement "auto-clickers" for idle gameplay&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Animate enemies when damaged&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3 id="buildamobileroadcrossinggameinunity"&gt;&lt;a id="buildamobileroadcrossinggameinunity" href="https://youtu.be/2CJG8j7KLyU"&gt;Build a Mobile Road Crossing Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master mobile game development with Unity by building a classic-styled road-crossing game. You will learn to implement common game mechanics such as collectibles, player movement, obstacles, and more with touch gestures and mobile screen sizes in mind. Not only will you discover how to alter and apply popular mechanics to work for mobile, but also gain design skills with the help of the Unity Device Simulator to demonstrate your project on various devices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Simulate various Android and iOS devices&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use swipe gestures to move players&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design maps and UIs for different screen sizes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement collectible coins&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up streams of moving enemies&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Script the camera to follow the player&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="constructafirstpersonshooterinunity"&gt;&lt;a id="constructafirstpersonshooterinunity" href="https://youtu.be/aIWn1HplrA0"&gt;Construct a First Person Shooter in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Develop your own FPS game in Unity!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;First-person shooters are not only immensely popular, but also one of the oldest genres in all of video game history. Through this course, you'll build your own FPS game in Unity while learning core mechanics for shooting, player movement, and similar. No matter how complex your planned features are, these FPS essentials will help put you on the path to building your dream FPS project!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create a moveable player character&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Master shooting mechanics with object pooling&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement pathfinding enemies with Unity NavMesh&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add health and ammo pickups&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up audio and particle effects&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop FPS-appropriate UIs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="createaretrolocalmultiplayergameinunity"&gt;&lt;a id="createaretrolocalmultiplayergameinunity" href="https://youtu.be/07iN3Ysw8bE"&gt;Create a Retro Local Multiplayer Game in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discover techniques for creating local multiplayer games with the popular Unity engine. Using Unity's Input System, you'll learn how to detect actions from different controllers and render multiple, nearby players to the same screen - all while creating a retro-styled, 2D action game. You'll not only master powerful features available with Unity's API, but gain game development knowledge that can be used to expand your single-player game projects in new directions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use Unity's Input System for control schemes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Detect different player controllers&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Spawn multiple players with different colors&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement combat detection between players&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up multiplayer-compatible UIs&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with particles and animations&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="createa3dturn-basedrpginunity"&gt;&lt;a id="createa3dturn-basedrpginunity" href="https://youtu.be/b93BS90N00M"&gt;Create a 3D Turn-Based RPG in Unity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master turn-based RPG combat - one of the most fundamental styles for the RPG genre.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turn-based combat is a mainstay for many RPGs due to its familiarity for players and the ease of implementation for developers. In this course, you'll master this combat style by building your own 3D RPG from scratch that features different kinds of attacks, customizable enemy encounters, and more. These skills will help you learn transferable skills in creating combat systems for many genres of projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will learn how to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Set up player and enemy sets&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Manage turns and action displays&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Implement different attacks &amp;amp; skills&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Create a simple, combat-ready enemy AI&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Add UI feedback for gameplay&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Build a map board with encounters&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;... and more&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
